        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Economic entomology is applied insect ecology: quantifying when insect populations cause economic harm and deploying biological, chemical, and cultural tools to manage them below damage thresholds. The dominant framework — Integrated Pest Management (IPM) — emerged in the 1960s as a reaction to the chemical pesticide paradigm and treats pest management as an optimization problem with ecological, economic, and toxicological constraints."
    },
