        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Economic Entomology: Pests and Biocontrol",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ECONOMIC THRESHOLDS:\n  EIL = Economic Injury Level: density at which crop loss = cost of control\n  ET  = Economic Threshold: action level (apply control BEFORE EIL to prevent crossing it)\n  ET always < EIL (by definition -- act before injury, not at injury)\n  ET varies by: crop value, control cost, pest growth rate, timing\n```"
    },
