        "title": "Economic Entomology: Pests and Biocontrol",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHITEFLIES (Hemiptera: Aleyrodidae)\n  Bemisia tabaci (biotype B = silverleaf whitefly):\n    Phloem feeder + major virus vector (Tomato Yellow Leaf Curl Virus, etc.)\n    B biotype: more virulent, more pesticide resistant than A biotype\n    Invasive globally (tropical origin; spread via ornamental trade)\n  Trialeurodes vaporariorum: greenhouse whitefly; temperate\n  Control: Encarsia formosa parasitoid, Beauveria bassiana, neonicotinoids"
    },
    {
