      "text": "ROOT/SOIL PESTS:\n  Diabrotica virgifera (western corn rootworm):\n    Most expensive pest in US agriculture; ~$1B/yr damage + control\n    Larvae: attack corn roots\n    Adults: silk feeding + leaf damage; vector of bacterial wilt\n    Resistance: to soil insecticides, Bt Cry3Bb1, crop rotation\n  Agriotes spp. (wireworms): click beetle larvae; soil; root crops"
