      "text": "TYPES:\n  CLASSICAL BIOLOGICAL CONTROL:\n    Import natural enemy from pest's native range\n    Release into new range (where pest has \"escaped\")\n    Target: invasive pests with no local natural enemies\n    Example: Aphytis melinus (chalcid wasp) vs California red scale\n             Rodolia cardinalis (ladybeetle) vs cottony cushion scale (1888)\n             Rodolia: first successful biocontrol; saved California citrus"
